.TH SRC 1
.SH NAME
src \- print the source path a compiled program was built from
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B src
.I name...
.SH DESCRIPTION
For each
.I name
(a
.B .dis
file or a bare program name resolved the same way the shell would),
.I src
reads the compiled module's own embedded metadata and prints the
source file path it was compiled from, or
.RB `` ? ''
if that could not be determined.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/src.b
